{% comment %}
  CRO-12473 — A3 short description (server-rendered in the Sprint 2 mount).
  cro-12473-pdp.js moves this into .product-block--short_desc (beneath the
  price).

  Per client decision (Donavan, Slack 2026-08-06): the blurb is the first
  150 characters of the PLAIN description text — all styling/headings
  stripped so it always reads as paragraph text — followed by a
  "Lees meer" link that anchors down to the "Oor hierdie produk" section
  (#cro-12473-description, rendered by cro-12473-description.liquid).

  @param short_text {String} plain, pre-truncated blurb text (never blank
    here — the section skips this render when there is no description)
{% endcomment %}
<div class="cro-12473-shortdesc" data-cro-12473-short-desc style="display: none;">
  <p>
    {{- short_text | escape }}
    <a class="cro-12473-readmore" href="#cro-12473-description">Lees meer</a>
  </p>
</div>
